Although some changes may be quite visible, others will require additional analysis.  When a significant
change occurs, the BIA should be updated with th e new information to identify new contingency
requirements or priorities.  As new technologies beco me available, preventive controls may be enhanced
and recovery strategies may be modified.  Finall y, plan maintenance should be continued as the
information system passes through the Disposal phase of  its life cycle to ensure that the plan accurately
reflects recovery priorities and concurrent processing changes.









































